    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To compute the value of \\(\\cos 150^\\circ\\), we recognize that it lies in the standard trigonometric table. Specifically, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 3(\\theta) = \\cos 3\\cdot(45^\\circ) = -2\\cos^3 45^\\circ - \\cos 45^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWhere \\(\\theta = 45^\\circ\\). Given that \\(\\cos 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\), we substitute and simplify:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -2 \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^3 - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = -2 \\cdot \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{8} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = -\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{4} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = -\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nCore concept: Trigonometric values are part of the standard values provided in the grading grading and determining their values in non-glittered values.\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\cos 150^\\circ\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]",
